.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dotman-apply 1  "apply "
.SH NAME
dotman\-apply \- Write the repo\*(Aqs files into $HOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotman apply\fR [\fB\-\-keep\-local\fR] [\fB\-\-take\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-forget\-deleted\fR] [\fB\-\-restore\-deleted\fR] [\fB\-\-accept\-identity\fR] [\fB\-\-approve\-hooks\fR] [\fB\-\-in\-place\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-hooks\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the repo\*(Aqs files into $HOME
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
Rewrite files in place when a rename cannot replace them, as on a bind mount
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-hooks\fR
Run no hooks
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be written and change nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-system\fR
Also write the system files outside $HOME, through one sudo, doas or run0 call
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
With \-\-system: write the system files without asking
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Apply only these files or directories, with \-\-system system files too; every managed path when none are given
.SH DECISIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-local\fR
Keep the local version of conflicting and existing files
.TP
\fB\-\-take\-repo\fR
Take the repo version of conflicting and existing files, after backing them up
.TP
\fB\-\-forget\-deleted\fR
Stop managing files deleted locally; they stay deleted
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\-deleted\fR
Write files deleted locally back from the repo
.TP
\fB\-\-accept\-identity\fR
Accept a changed machine identity and use the variants it selects
.TP
\fB\-\-approve\-hooks\fR
Approve the current `[hooks]` table on this machine and run its hooks
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
Allow running as root
